<title>FINLAND: FINNISH JULY EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS RISE 5.7 PCT.</title>
<headline>FINNISH JULY EXPORTS THROUGH PORTS RISE 5.7 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish exports through ports rose 5.7 percent year-on-year in July to 2.60 million tonnes, the Board of Navigation said in a statement on Thursday.  </p>
<p>In January-July, exports through ports fell 9.9 percent year-on-year to 18.91 million tonnes.</p>
<p>July imports through ports rose 6.3 percent to 3.23 million tonnes but January-July imports fell 4.6 percent to 19.50 million tonnes, the board said.  </p>
<p>The Board of Navigation gave the following statistics of</p>
<p>foreign trade via ports (thousands of tonnes):</p>
<p>EXPORTS</p>
<p>			 ---------- 1996 ----------    --- 1995------</p>
<p>			 July	June    Jan-July   July   Jan-July</p>
<p>  TOTAL		2,604     2,717   18,908     2,466  20,654</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>  Paper		652	 646     4,467	668    5,167</p>
<p>  Pulp		 108	 141     828	  105	755</p>
<p>  Sawn goods	 228	 309     2,043	229    2,280</p>
<p>  Chemicals	  182	 129     1,247	231    1,908</p>
<p>Metals,</p>
<p>  metal products   163	 189     1,237	156    1,538</p>
<p>IMPORTS</p>
<p>			 ---------- 1996 ----------    --- 1995 ---</p>
<p>			  July	June    Jan-July    July  Jan-July</p>
<p>  TOTAL		 3,235     3,020   19,504	3,113 20,356</p>
<p>of which</p>
<p>  Crude oil	   551	 568	3,829	804   4,353</p>
<p>  Oil products	500	 296	2,255	188   1,708</p>
<p>  Raw minerals,     290	 274	1,814	372   2,148</p>
<p>cement</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
